            <ArticleTitle>Arginase: marker, effector, or candidate gene for asthma?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1815-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Microarray analysis of the expression profiles of lung tissue in two murine models of asthma revealed high levels of arginase I and arginase II activity, in association with IL-4 and IL-13 overexpression, suggesting that arginine pathways are critical in the pathogenesis of asthma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
